        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{1}^{5}\\frac{7{log}_{5}(5\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\log_{5}\\left(5 \\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\right).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{1}^{5}\\frac{7{log}_{5}(5\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{14}{5}\\int_{1}^{5}{log}_{5}(5\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{14}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{14 \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(7\\operatorname{ln}5\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}\\right)|_{1}^{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(7\\operatorname{ln}5\\cdot (\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{21\\operatorname{ln}5}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
